        "question": {
          ":question/id": "10f3b11d-2af3-58c6-90e4-60c9e13df639",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
          ":question/problem": "Given $q=\u27e8-6,-10,10\u27e9$ and $r=\u27e8-1,7,-7\u27e9.$\n\nFind the dot product of the vectors $q$ and $r.$\n\n$q\\cdot r=\\,$ {{field-1}}",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The dot product of two vectors given in component form can be computed by summing up the products of corresponding components of vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & ={q}_{x}\\cdot {r}_{x}+{q}_{y}\\cdot {r}_{y}+{q}_{z}\\cdot {r}_{z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor these vectors, we have $q=\u27e8-6,-10,10\u27e9$ and $r=\u27e8-1,7,-7\u27e9.$ Therefore, the formula for the dot product gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q\\cdot r & =(-6)\\cdot (-1)+(-10)\\cdot 7+10\\cdot (-7) \\\\  & =6-70-70 \\\\  & =-134.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          ":question/answer-fields": [
            {
              ":answer-field/id": "06601d94-0b38-570c-8cff-9783e6862173",
